--[[
    MM2 SKIN ENGINE  (module)

    Ported from the standalone "MM2 Spawner + Weapon Visualizer" script so
    Nely Hub can drive it instead of that script's own floating GUI. The
    engine itself is unchanged; only the GUI is removed and a small API is
    added at the bottom.

    How it actually works, because the obvious approach does not:

      * SPAWN writes ProfileData.Weapons.Owned directly. MM2's inventory
        reads that table, so the item becomes real to every client-side
        reader. Firing ChangeInventoryItem's client event instead only
        spoofs a signal, which is why that approach lets an item appear
        and then refuse to equip.

      * EQUIP is detected by POLLING ProfileData.Weapons.Equipped, because
        InventoryModule writes that field and fires the remote directly --
        it never calls EquipService.EquipItem, so EquippedChanged does not
        fire and an event-only listener misses every real equip.

      * RENDER cannot reuse the game's assets: MM2 ships no skin models to
        the client, and will not render a skin it does not believe you
        own. So the engine carries its own scraped mesh trees and welds a
        built overlay over the weapon -- the tool Handle in a round, the
        DisplayRef in the lobby -- hiding the original underneath.

      * CHROMA is a real MM2 mechanic driven by the ChromaDecal /
        ChromaPart / ChromaFire CollectionService tags; the overlay carries
        those over and animates them.

    Client-side only. The server keeps its own inventory and is not fooled:
    nothing here survives a rejoin, replicates to other players, or works
    in a trade.
--]]

local CONFIG = {
    InjectParticles = true,   -- ParticleEmitter / Fire / Smoke / Sparkles / Lights
    HideOriginal    = true,   -- hide your real held weapon so only the spawn shows
    PollRate        = 0.1,    -- how often to check for an equip change (seconds)
}

local Players           = game:GetService("Players")
local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
local InsertService     = game:GetService("InsertService")
local LocalPlayer       = Players.LocalPlayer

pcall(function() if setthreadidentity then setthreadidentity(2) end end)

-- re-runnable: tear down any previous instance
if _G.__MM2Viz and _G.__MM2Viz.destroy then pcall(_G.__MM2Viz.destroy) end
local SELF = { conns = {} }
_G.__MM2Viz = SELF

local ClientServices = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("ClientServices")
local EquipService = require(ClientServices:WaitForChild("EquipService"))
local Sync         = require(ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Database"):WaitForChild("Sync"))
local ProfileData  = require(ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Modules"):WaitForChild("ProfileData"))
local WeaponDB     = Sync.Weapons -- == Sync.Item (full weapon database)
local Remotes      = ReplicatedStorage:WaitForChild("Remotes")
local InvDataChanged = Remotes:WaitForChild("Inventory"):WaitForChild("InventoryDataChanged")

